# Windows-native implementation

When the user asks to **fix/update the desktop app**, also follow `.cursor/skills/fix-desktop/SKILL.md` and [`docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md`](../../docs/PWA_DESKTOP_COMPAT.md).

Windows-native code belongs in:

- `src-tauri/` — Tauri 2 shell, IPC commands, packaging
- `desktop/sidecar/` — packaged Python / GDAL / PDAL
- `js/platform/windows/` — **only** place allowed to import `@tauri-apps/*`

## Rules

- Expose native behavior through **narrow typed service operations** (not generic shell or `runPythonScript`)
- Every native operation needs: input validation, structured errors, progress, cancellation, temp-file cleanup
- Changes must **not** break the public web build (`npm run build` / `npm run build:web`)
- Do not require end users to install system Python, GDAL, or PDAL
- Long-running work goes through the job service contract (`ctx.services.jobs`)
- Keep secrets out of packaged desktop files — use backend proxy / Credential Manager / user credentials
